**Gates before launch**

I check four gates before I call the Workflow. First, `git log -- spe/predictions/r04.yaml spe/plans/r04.md` must show the predict commit, and `git status` must show both files clean. The script's Setup phase checks this again and stops if it fails. Second, I run the grader selftest. answers.json used as the oracle must pass on label.category and label.priority, and an empty answer and a wrong answer must fail. I also give the judge one good reply and one rude reply. It must pass the first and fail the second. Third, I regrade round 3's raw outputs with the round 4 grade.py and compare the scores to round 3's published numbers. If those numbers change, the grader changed, and I report that before I trust any round 4 result. Fourth, I do a dry run with `args.only` set to `["B:T001","C2:T001","C2:T017"]` and `trialsPerCell: 1`. Every phase must return valid output, the leak scan must run, and the ledger must show a real spend. When all four gates pass, I commit `SPE r04 evaluate (harness): ...` and only then start the full run.

**Assumptions to check against r03-workflow.js.** I wrote this from the prompt alone and did not read round 3's script. So the runner command (`args.runner`), its stdout field names, and grade.py's CLI are guesses. The grade agent reads `--help` first to work around the CLI guess. The plan does not give `estRunUsd` or `topUpTrials`, so set both from r04.md. The $40 cap covers runner API spend as each run reports it. Harness agents are capped by `maxTrialAgents` instead. I also guessed that `meta.phases` takes plain strings.

```js
export const meta = {
  name: 'spe-r04-eval',
  description: 'SPE round 4: configs B and C2 on 50 tickets, 5 trials per cell, code grader for label.category and label.priority, Opus judge for reply tone, $40 spend cap',
  phases: ['Setup', 'Trials', 'Grade', 'Top-up', 'Judge', 'Synthesis'],
};

// ---------- Round and arguments ----------
const ROUND = 'r04';

const DEFAULTS = {
  configs: ['B', 'C2'],
  expectedTickets: 50,
  trialsPerCell: 5,
  topUpTrials: 5,            // cap on extra trials per partial-pass cell. Set from r04.md.
  spendCapUsd: 40,
  estRunUsd: 0.06,           // reserved per runner call before launch. Set from r04.md.
  maxTrialAgents: 220,
  concurrency: 10,
  only: null,                // dry run, e.g. ['B:T001', 'C2:T001', 'C2:T017']
  runner: 'python spe/run_config.py',
  workerModel: 'opus',
  judgeModel: 'opus',
  judgeSeed: ROUND,
};
const A = Object.assign({}, DEFAULTS, (typeof args === 'object' && args) ? args : {});
const DRY = Array.isArray(A.only) && A.only.length > 0;
const OUT = DRY ? `spe/evals/results/${ROUND}-dryrun` : `spe/evals/results/${ROUND}`;
const RAW = `${OUT}/raw`;

// Used in logs and the report only. Never shown to the judge.
const CONFIG_NOTES = {
  B: '12-line prompt, 6 tools',
  C2: '12-line prompt, 3 tools plus a separate check_status tool',
};

const FORBIDDEN = ['spe/evals/', 'spe/predictions/', 'spe/plans/', 'spe/spec/', 'spe/prediction-log.md', 'spe/failures.md'];
const ANSWER_KEY = ['spe/evals/tasks/answers.json', 'spe/evals/graders/', 'spe/predictions/'];

// ---------- Schemas ----------
const SETUP_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['predictionsCommitted', 'ticketIds'],
  properties: {
    predictionsCommitted: { type: 'boolean' },
    predictionsCommit: { type: 'string' },
    ticketIds: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    note: { type: 'string' },
  },
};

const TRIAL_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['runs', 'pathsIOpened'],
  properties: {
    runs: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['trial', 'status'],
        properties: {
          trial: { type: 'integer' },
          status: { type: 'string', enum: ['completed', 'harness_error', 'rate_limited'] },
          category: { type: 'string' },
          priority: { type: 'string' },
          reply: { type: 'string' },
          runtimeMs: { type: 'number' },
          toolCalls: { type: 'number' },
          tokensIn: { type: 'number' },
          tokensOut: { type: 'number' },
          toolErrors: { type: 'number' },
          costUsd: { type: 'number' },
          transcriptPath: { type: 'string' },
          sutPathsRead: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
          error: { type: 'string' },
        },
      },
    },
    pathsIOpened: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  },
};

const GRADE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['graderOk', 'results', 'transcriptPeeks'],
  properties: {
    graderOk: { type: 'boolean' },
    graderNote: { type: 'string' },
    results: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['outPath', 'categoryOk', 'priorityOk'],
        properties: {
          outPath: { type: 'string' },
          categoryOk: { type: 'boolean' },
          priorityOk: { type: 'boolean' },
          expectedCategory: { type: 'string' },
          expectedPriority: { type: 'string' },
        },
      },
    },
    transcriptPeeks: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['outPath', 'pathRead'],
        properties: { outPath: { type: 'string' }, pathRead: { type: 'string' } },
      },
    },
  },
};

const JUDGE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['scores'],
  properties: {
    scores: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['id', 'score', 'pass', 'reason'],
        properties: {
          id: { type: 'string' },
          score: { type: 'number' },
          pass: { type: 'boolean' },
          reason: { type: 'string' },
        },
      },
    },
  },
};

const ANALYSIS_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['modes'],
  properties: {
    modes: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['name', 'count', 'configs', 'examples'],
        properties: {
          name: { type: 'string' },
          count: { type: 'integer' },
          configs: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
          examples: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
          likelyCause: { type: 'string' },
        },
      },
    },
  },
};

const CRITIC_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['complete', 'gaps'],
  properties: {
    complete: { type: 'boolean' },
    gaps: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    measuredNothing: { type: 'boolean' },
  },
};

const WRITE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['written'],
  properties: { written: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } } },
};

// ---------- Helpers ----------
const ledger = { spentUsd: 0, reservedUsd: 0, trialAgents: 0, skipped: [] };
let halted = null;

function skip(what, why) {
  ledger.skipped.push(`${what} (${why})`);
  log(`Skipped ${what}: ${why}`);
}

function hits(paths, allow) {
  return (paths || []).filter((p) => FORBIDDEN.some((f) => p.includes(f)) && !allow.includes(p));
}

function isKey(p) {
  return ANSWER_KEY.some((k) => p.includes(k));
}

function hash(s) {
  let h = 2166136261;
  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {
    h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);
    h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);
  }
  return h >>> 0;
}

const pct = (x) => (x == null ? 'n/a' : `${(100 * x).toFixed(1)}%`);
const num = (x, d = 2) => (x == null ? 'n/a' : Number(x).toFixed(d));

async function inBatches(items, size, fn) {
  const out = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i += size) {
    const chunk = items.slice(i, i + size);
    const res = await parallel(chunk.map((it) => () => fn(it)));
    out.push(...res);
  }
  return out;
}

// ---------- Trial runner ----------
async function runCell(cell, firstTrial, n, phaseName) {
  const what = `${cell.key} t${firstTrial}-t${firstTrial + n - 1}`;
  if (halted) { skip(what, `round halted: ${halted}`); return []; }
  if (ledger.trialAgents >= A.maxTrialAgents) { skip(what, `trial agent cap ${A.maxTrialAgents}`); return []; }
  const reserve = n * A.estRunUsd;
  if (ledger.spentUsd + ledger.reservedUsd + reserve > A.spendCapUsd) {
    halted = halted || `spend cap $${A.spendCapUsd} would be crossed`;
    skip(what, halted);
    return [];
  }
  // Reserve before the first await so parallel thunks cannot overspend.
  ledger.reservedUsd += reserve;
  ledger.trialAgents += 1;

  const trials = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => firstTrial + i);
  const outPath = (t) => `${RAW}/${cell.cfg}/${cell.id}/t${t}.json`;
  const cmds = trials.map(
    (t) => `${A.runner} --round ${ROUND} --config ${cell.cfg} --ticket ${cell.id} --trial ${t} --out ${outPath(t)}`
  );

  const prompt = [
    'You are a harness worker for an eval. You run a fixed command and copy its output. You do not judge, fix, or retry beyond one retry.',
    '',
    'Allowed reads: the stdout and stderr of the commands below. Nothing else.',
    'Forbidden: do not open, cat, grep, list, or search any path under spe/. That includes spe/evals/, spe/predictions/, spe/plans/, and spe/spec/. Do not read the files the command writes. A trial that reads these paths is voided.',
    '',
    'Run these commands one at a time, in order:',
    ...cmds,
    '',
    'Each command prints one JSON object on stdout with these fields: status, label.category, label.priority, reply, runtime_ms, tool_calls, tokens_in, tokens_out, tool_errors, cost_usd, transcript_path, paths_read.',
    'Copy them into your result without changing them. Use trial = the --trial number. Map paths_read to sutPathsRead.',
    'If a command exits non-zero or times out, set status "harness_error" and put the error text in error. If it hits a rate limit, set status "rate_limited". Retry at most once, then move on.',
    'In pathsIOpened, list every file path you opened or listed yourself. Return an empty list if there are none.',
  ].join('\n');

  let res = null;
  let err = null;
  try {
    res = await agent(prompt, {
      label: `${phaseName} ${cell.key} t${firstTrial}-t${firstTrial + n - 1}`,
      phase: phaseName,
      schema: TRIAL_SCHEMA,
      model: A.workerModel,
    });
  } catch (e) {
    err = String(e);
  }

  // When the worker fails, the real spend is unknown, so count the full reserve as spent.
  const actual = res ? res.runs.reduce((s, r) => s + (Number(r.costUsd) || 0), 0) : reserve;
  ledger.reservedUsd -= reserve;
  ledger.spentUsd += actual;

  if (!res) {
    log(`Harness error on ${cell.key}: ${err}`);
    return trials.map((t) => ({
      key: cell.key, cfg: cell.cfg, id: cell.id, trial: t, base: t <= A.trialsPerCell,
      outPath: outPath(t), status: 'harness_error', error: err, voided: false,
    }));
  }

  const workerPeek = hits(res.pathsIOpened, []);
  return trials.map((t) => {
    const r = res.runs.find((x) => x.trial === t) || { trial: t, status: 'harness_error', error: 'worker did not report this trial' };
    const peek = workerPeek.concat(hits(r.sutPathsRead, [outPath(t)]));
    if (peek.some(isKey)) halted = halted || `answer key leaked to ${cell.key} t${t}`;
    return {
      ...r,
      key: cell.key, cfg: cell.cfg, id: cell.id, trial: t, base: t <= A.trialsPerCell,
      outPath: outPath(t),
      voided: peek.length > 0,
      voidReason: peek.length ? `read ${peek.join(', ')}` : null,
    };
  });
}

// ---------- Grader ----------
async function grade(runs, tag, phaseName) {
  const targets = runs.filter((r) => r.status === 'completed' && !r.voided);
  if (!targets.length) return;
  let res;
  try {
    res = await agent([
      `You grade eval outputs for SPE round ${ROUND}. You run code. You never grade by hand.`,
      '',
      'Step 1. Run `python spe/evals/graders/grade.py --help` and use its real interface.',
      'Step 2. Run the grader selftest. The oracle answer must pass. The empty and wrong answers must fail. If any of these is wrong, or grade.py will not run, set graderOk to false and explain in graderNote.',
      'Step 3. Grade exactly these output files against spe/evals/tasks/answers.json. Each file holds label.category and label.priority:',
      ...targets.map((r) => r.outPath),
      `Step 4. Save grade.py's raw output to ${OUT}/graded-${tag}.json.`,
      'Step 5. Leak scan. For each file above, open the transcript at its transcript_path field. Report any tool call that reads, lists, or searches a path under spe/evals/, spe/predictions/, spe/plans/, or spe/spec/. Ignore the runner writing its own output file.',
      '',
      'Do not edit grade.py, answers.json, or any output file.',
    ].join('\n'), { label: `Grade ${tag}`, phase: phaseName, schema: GRADE_SCHEMA, model: A.workerModel });
  } catch (e) {
    halted = halted || `grader agent failed: ${String(e)}`;
    return;
  }

  if (!res.graderOk) {
    halted = halted || `grader broken mid-run: ${res.graderNote || 'no note'}`;
    log(halted);
  }
  for (const p of res.transcriptPeeks) {
    const r = targets.find((x) => x.outPath === p.outPath);
    if (!r) continue;
    r.voided = true;
    r.voidReason = `transcript read ${p.pathRead}`;
    if (isKey(p.pathRead)) halted = halted || `answer key leaked to ${r.key} t${r.trial}`;
  }
  for (const r of targets) {
    const g = res.results.find((x) => x.outPath === r.outPath);
    if (!g) { r.status = 'ungraded'; continue; }
    r.graded = true;
    r.categoryOk = g.categoryOk;
    r.priorityOk = g.priorityOk;
    r.expectedCategory = g.expectedCategory;
    r.expectedPriority = g.expectedPriority;
  }
}

// ---------- Judge (blind, one agent per ticket) ----------
async function judgeTicket(id, runs) {
  const items = runs
    .filter((r) => r.id === id && r.status === 'completed' && !r.voided && r.reply)
    .map((r) => ({ jid: 'R' + hash(`${A.judgeSeed}|${r.outPath}`).toString(36), run: r }))
    .sort((a, b) => (a.jid < b.jid ? -1 : 1));
  if (!items.length) return;
  try {
    const res = await agent([
      'You judge the tone of customer support replies.',
      'Read spe/evals/graders/judge.md and apply its rubric exactly.',
      `Read the ticket text for ${id} from the ticket file in spe/evals/tasks/. Do not open answers.json.`,
      'Do not open anything under spe/evals/results/, spe/predictions/, or spe/plans/.',
      'The replies below come from different setups in shuffled order. Judge each one alone.',
      'Score each reply on the scale judge.md defines. Set pass as judge.md defines it. Give a one-sentence reason.',
      '',
      ...items.map((it) => `--- ${it.jid} ---\n${JSON.stringify(it.run.reply)}`),
    ].join('\n'), { label: `Judge ${id}`, phase: 'Judge', schema: JUDGE_SCHEMA, model: A.judgeModel });
    for (const s of res.scores) {
      const it = items.find((i) => i.jid === s.id);
      if (it) it.run.tone = { score: s.score, pass: s.pass, reason: s.reason };
    }
  } catch (e) {
    log(`Judge failed on ${id}: ${String(e)}`);
  }
}

// ---------- Metrics ----------
function summarize(runs, cells) {
  const pass = (r) => r.categoryOk && r.priorityOk;
  const mean = (xs, f) => (xs.length ? xs.reduce((s, r) => s + (Number(f(r)) || 0), 0) / xs.length : null);
  const rate = (xs, f) => (xs.length ? xs.filter(f).length / xs.length : null);
  const out = {};
  for (const cfg of A.configs) {
    const rs = runs.filter((r) => r.cfg === cfg);
    // Count only completed, graded, non-voided trials.
    const done = rs.filter((r) => r.status === 'completed' && !r.voided && r.graded);
    // Base trials keep equal weight per ticket and match the prediction. Top-up trials only refine per-ticket rates.
    const base = done.filter((r) => r.base);
    const cellRates = cells
      .filter((c) => c.cfg === cfg)
      .map((c) => rate(done.filter((r) => r.key === c.key), pass))
      .filter((x) => x !== null);
    const judged = base.filter((r) => r.tone);
    out[cfg] = {
      config: CONFIG_NOTES[cfg],
      completedBase: base.length,
      completedAll: done.length,
      harnessErrors: rs.filter((r) => r.status !== 'completed').length,
      voided: rs.filter((r) => r.voided).length,
      passRateBase: rate(base, pass),
      passRatePerTicketAllTrials: cellRates.length ? cellRates.reduce((s, x) => s + x, 0) / cellRates.length : null,
      categoryAcc: rate(base, (r) => r.categoryOk),
      priorityAcc: rate(base, (r) => r.priorityOk),
      tonePassRate: rate(judged, (r) => r.tone.pass),
      toneMean: mean(judged, (r) => r.tone.score),
      judgeCoverage: base.length ? judged.length / base.length : null,
      meanRuntimeMs: mean(base, (r) => r.runtimeMs),
      meanToolCalls: mean(base, (r) => r.toolCalls),
      meanTokens: mean(base, (r) => (r.tokensIn || 0) + (r.tokensOut || 0)),
      meanToolErrors: mean(base, (r) => r.toolErrors),
      meanCostUsd: mean(base, (r) => r.costUsd),
    };
  }
  return out;
}

// ---------- Setup ----------
phase('Setup');
log(`SPE ${ROUND}. Configs: ${A.configs.map((c) => `${c} (${CONFIG_NOTES[c]})`).join(', ')}. Cap $${A.spendCapUsd}. Output ${OUT}.${DRY ? ' DRY RUN.' : ''}`);
log('Judge is Opus. If the system under test is also Claude, the judge shares its model family. No cross-family judge is available in this harness, so read tone results with that blind spot in mind.');

const setup = await agent([
  `You check preconditions for SPE round ${ROUND}. Report facts only.`,
  `1. Run git log -1 --format=%H -- spe/predictions/${ROUND}.yaml and git status --porcelain spe/predictions/${ROUND}.yaml.`,
  '   predictionsCommitted is true only if a commit exists and the file has no uncommitted changes. Do not read the file contents.',
  '2. List the ticket IDs from the ticket file in spe/evals/tasks/. Do not open answers.json. Return the IDs only.',
].join('\n'), { label: 'Setup', phase: 'Setup', schema: SETUP_SCHEMA, model: A.workerModel });

if (!setup.predictionsCommitted) {
  throw new Error(`spe/predictions/${ROUND}.yaml is missing or uncommitted. Write and commit the prediction first.`);
}
if (!DRY && setup.ticketIds.length !== A.expectedTickets) {
  throw new Error(`Expected ${A.expectedTickets} tickets, found ${setup.ticketIds.length}. The approved plan says ${A.expectedTickets}.`);
}

let cells = [];
for (const cfg of A.configs) {
  for (const id of setup.ticketIds) cells.push({ key: `${cfg}:${id}`, cfg, id });
}
if (DRY) cells = cells.filter((c) => A.only.includes(c.key));
log(`${cells.length} cells, ${A.trialsPerCell} trials each.`);

// ---------- Trials ----------
phase('Trials');
const runs = (await inBatches(cells, A.concurrency, (c) => runCell(c, 1, A.trialsPerCell, 'Trials'))).flat();
log(`Trials done. ${runs.length} runs. Spent $${num(ledger.spentUsd)}.`);

// ---------- Grade ----------
phase('Grade');
await grade(runs, 'base', 'Grade');
log(`Graded ${runs.filter((r) => r.graded).length}. Voided ${runs.filter((r) => r.voided).length}.${halted ? ` HALTED: ${halted}` : ''}`);

// ---------- Top-up ----------
phase('Top-up');
if (halted) {
  log(`Top-up skipped. Round halted: ${halted}`);
} else {
  const partial = cells.filter((c) => {
    const done = runs.filter((r) => r.key === c.key && r.graded && !r.voided);
    const passes = done.filter((r) => r.categoryOk && r.priorityOk).length;
    return done.length > 0 && passes > 0 && passes < done.length;
  });
  log(`${partial.length} partial-pass cells get up to ${A.topUpTrials} extra trials each.`);
  const extra = (await inBatches(partial, A.concurrency, (c) => runCell(c, A.trialsPerCell + 1, A.topUpTrials, 'Top-up'))).flat();
  await grade(extra, 'topup', 'Top-up');
  runs.push(...extra);
}

// ---------- Judge ----------
phase('Judge');
if (halted) {
  log(`Judge skipped. Round halted: ${halted}`);
} else {
  const ids = [...new Set(cells.map((c) => c.id))];
  await inBatches(ids, A.concurrency, (id) => judgeTicket(id, runs));
}

// ---------- Synthesis ----------
phase('Synthesis');
const summary = summarize(runs, cells);
const measuredNothing = A.configs.every((c) => summary[c].passRateBase === 1 && summary[c].tonePassRate === 1);
if (measuredNothing) log('Every configuration passed everything. This round measured nothing. The next round needs harder tasks or stricter graders.');

const headline = A.configs
  .map((c) => `${c} ${pct(summary[c].passRateBase)} label, ${pct(summary[c].tonePassRate)} tone, $${num(summary[c].meanCostUsd, 3)}/task`)
  .join(' | ');

const report = {
  round: ROUND,
  dryRun: DRY,
  halted,
  measuredNothing,
  headline,
  budget: { capUsd: A.spendCapUsd, spentUsd: ledger.spentUsd, trialAgents: ledger.trialAgents, skipped: ledger.skipped },
  summary,
  cells: cells.map((c) => {
    const done = runs.filter((r) => r.key === c.key && r.graded && !r.voided);
    return { key: c.key, completed: done.length, passes: done.filter((r) => r.categoryOk && r.priorityOk).length };
  }),
};

await agent([
  `Write two files for SPE round ${ROUND}. Do not change any number.`,
  `1. ${OUT}/summary.json with exactly this JSON:`,
  JSON.stringify(report, null, 2),
  `2. ${OUT}/report.md with a table of the summary (one column per config, one row per metric), then the budget, the skipped list, and the halt reason if there is one.`,
], { label: 'Write results', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: WRITE_SCHEMA, model: A.workerModel });

const failures = runs
  .filter((r) => r.graded && !r.voided && (!(r.categoryOk && r.priorityOk) || (r.tone && !r.tone.pass)))
  .map((r) => ({
    cell: r.key, trial: r.trial, outPath: r.outPath, transcriptPath: r.transcriptPath,
    got: { category: r.category, priority: r.priority },
    expected: { category: r.expectedCategory, priority: r.expectedPriority },
    tone: r.tone || null,
  }));

const analysis = await agent([
  `You analyze failures from SPE round ${ROUND}. Group them into failure modes.`,
  'For each mode, give a name, a count, the configs it hits, 2 or 3 example cells with trial numbers, and a likely cause you can point to in the transcript.',
  'Read the output files and transcripts listed below as needed.',
  `Write your findings to ${OUT}/failure-analysis.md. Do not edit spe/failures.md. The learn step does that.`,
  '',
  JSON.stringify(failures, null, 2),
].join('\n'), { label: 'Failure analysis', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: ANALYSIS_SCHEMA, model: A.workerModel });

const critic = await agent([
  `You are the completeness critic for SPE round ${ROUND}. Find what is missing or untrustworthy in this run.`,
  `Check these points: cells with fewer than ${A.trialsPerCell} completed base trials, voided trials, harness errors, skipped work, judge coverage below 100%, a halt reason, and whether every configuration passed everything.`,
  'Also check that the failure analysis accounts for every failure.',
  `Write your findings to ${OUT}/critic.md.`,
  '',
  'Report:',
  JSON.stringify(report, null, 2),
  '',
  'Failure analysis:',
  JSON.stringify(analysis, null, 2),
].join('\n'), { label: 'Completeness critic', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: CRITIC_SCHEMA, model: A.workerModel });

log(`Headline: ${headline}`);
if (halted) log(`ROUND HALTED: ${halted}. Results are partial. Report this before any comparison.`);

return {
  round: ROUND,
  halted,
  headline,
  suggestedCommit: `SPE ${ROUND} evaluate (results): ${headline}`,
  summary,
  spentUsd: ledger.spentUsd,
  skipped: ledger.skipped,
  critic,
  failureModes: analysis.modes,
};
```
